A file that states its own license in an SPDX-License-Identifier line is
governed by that license. Every other folder and file of this repository is
proprietary to Cernanto: no license, express or implied, is granted to it,
and copying, modification, distribution or use is prohibited without prior
written permission from Cernanto.

The BSL Additional Use Grant permits production use except offering the
Licensed Work to third parties on a hosted or embedded basis as a competitive
offering. A competitive offering is a paid Product that significantly overlaps
the agent or workflow platform capabilities defined in the grant. A paid basis
includes the Product provider's charges for required infrastructure or usage,
or support covering the Product, whether charged separately or as part of a
broader offering. Products include hosted or managed services, including in
customer-supplied environments, and software customers operate themselves.
Embedded use includes requiring the Licensed Work to be accessed or downloaded
for a Product to operate.

Internal use, including use within affiliates under common control, is
expressly permitted. Assisting a customer with its own permitted use does not,
by itself, make a competitive offering; a Product offered with those services
is still assessed under the grant. Using the engine as an internal application
component does not, by itself, make the application competitive. The comparison
concerns the platform capabilities offered to customers, including within a
larger Product.

Products not provided on a paid basis are not competitive. A Product that was
not competitive when first made generally available does not become competitive
later merely because Cernanto adds capabilities. The standard BSL rights to
copy, modify, redistribute and make non-production use remain unchanged. This
is a summary; each folder's LICENSE file contains the governing terms.

Separately licensed components, including any enterprise components, remain
governed by their own terms and are outside the BSL grant. The Cernanto Output
Exception protects customer application outputs; it does not relicense the
compiler, runtime or platform implementations distributed with them.

Cernanto's compiler and runtime are the subject of a pending patent
application. The Apache-licensed components carry the patent license in
section 3 of Apache License, Version 2.0.

For the BSL-licensed components, Cernanto will not assert any patent it owns
or controls against use of the Licensed Work permitted by the applicable
License and Additional Use Grant. This includes using the Licensed Work to
compile, deploy and run customer agents and generated application outputs.
The commitment does not extend to patent claims infringed independently of
that permitted use, and does not prevent defense against a party that first
brings a patent claim against Cernanto. Nothing in this statement narrows the
Apache patent license.

